      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:202:9",
      "text": [
        " رَأَيْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) قَدْ دَخَلَ الْكَعْبَةَ ثُمَّ أَرَادَ بَيْنَ الْعَمُودَيْنِ فَلَمْ يَقْدِرْ عَلَيْهِ فَصَلَّى دُونَهُ ثُمَّ خَرَجَ فَمَضَى حَتَّى خَرَجَ مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And from hi, from Ibn Fazzal, from Yunus Bin Yaqoub who said, ",
          "‘I saw Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> entering the Kabah, then intended to be between the two pillars, but was not able upon doing so, so he<sup>asws</sup> Prayed <span class=\"iTxt\">Salaat</span> besides it. Then he<sup>asws</sup> exited, so he<sup>asws</sup> went until he had gone out from the Masjid’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "9. It is narrated from him (narrator of previous Hadith) from ibn Faddal from Yunus ibn Ya’qub who has said the following: “I saw abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, enter al-Ka‘bah and he (the Imam) wanted between the two pillars; but could not get there, he (the Imam) then performed Salat (prayer) nearby, then went out and continued walking until he left the Masjid.” "
        ]
      }
    },
